<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zeil Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Schloss Zeil</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zeil Castle (Schloss Zeil) is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> castle on a hill near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leutkirch-im-allgau">Leutkirch im Allgäu</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-swabia">Upper Swabia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Built in the late 16th and early 17th centuries on the site of an older fortress, it is the seat of the princes of Waldburg-Zeil, one of the main branches of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-waldburg">House of Waldburg</a>, who ruled the surrounding county until its mediatisation in 1806.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zeil-castle.jpg" alt="Zeil Castle" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flodur63 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leutkirch_-_Schloss_Zeil_-_Leutkirch_v_N_08.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
